{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Root cause confirmed (AC1); full chain in the description. The frame that enumerates `%TEMP%` is pytest's `Session.collect` (`_pytest/main.py`, identical in 9.0.3 and the runner's 9.2.0). With rootdir and confcutdir stuck on the `D:` repo, every `C:` ancestor of the tmp_path test file is collected, and on `win32` each scanned entry goes through `samefile_nofollow` -> `Path.lstat()`. A `rebar-ticket-view-*` sibling removed by another worker raises FileNotFoundError. Reproduced on macOS by forcing `win32` matching and removing a sibling after its parent's scan: rc 2, `ERROR collecting test session`. Each of the 3 controls passes.\n\nFix (commit a28027d5ec7, worktree a4-nested-pytest-rootdir): `run_nested_pytest` adds `--rootdir <the arguments' directory>` when every existing absolute path argument lies outside the child's cwd and the caller chose no rootdir, config file or confcutdir.\nRED/GREEN (AC2, no Windows needed): without the pin, the 6 new tests fail. The end-to-end one fails with `ImportError while loading conftest ... RuntimeError: collection walked above the test dir`. With it, all 30 helper tests pass.\nPOSIX impact measured: the 19 modules that call the helper gave 223 passed, 2 skipped before and after, with a basetemp sharing a non-root ancestor with the checkout (the Linux CI layout).\nPortability: os.path/ntpath string logic plus exists/isdir only; a cross-drive ValueError is caught."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1795115811114289980,"uuid":"a97599f3-c6c6-431a-9de1-d29ce6c4b3c3"}